  "estimatedMinutes": 2,
  "statement": "The set of values of \\(m\\) for which \\(x^2+3xy+x+my-m\\) has two factors, with integer coefficients, which are linear in \\(x\\) and \\(y,\\) is precisely:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(0,\\) \\(12,\\) \\(-12\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(0,\\) \\(12\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(12,\\) \\(-12\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(12\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(0\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1964-p25.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Write the factorization as \\((x+ay+b)(x+cy+d).\\) Comparing the \\(y^2\\) and \\(xy\\) coefficients gives \\(ac=0\\) and \\(a+c=3,\\) so take \\(a=0,\\) \\(c=3.\\) The other coefficients give \\[ \\begin{aligned} b+d&=1,\\\\ bd&=-m,\\\\ 3b&=m. \\end{aligned} \\] Hence \\(b(d+3)=0.\\) If \\(b=0,\\) then \\(m=0;\\) otherwise \\(d=-3,\\) \\(b=4,\\) and \\(m=12.\\) Both values produce valid integer factorizations.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Write the factors as \\((x+ay+b)(x+cy+d)\\)",
        "The missing \\(y^2\\)-term and the \\(3xy\\)-term force \\(\\{a,c\\}=\\{0,3\\}\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
